 Messages exist in English (`en`) and Korean (`ko`), in
 `src/i18n/messages.js`. The server answers in `LARDER_LANG` (default `en`).
+
+## Till sales
+
+`POST /import/sales` accepts a JSON object with a `csv` string containing the
+columns `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty`. Supply an ISO instant with a time zone and
+a positive whole-number quantity. Each dish uses one recipe portion.
+The response contains `tickets` (distinct newly imported tickets) and
+`dishes` (total portions sold on those tickets). Previously imported tickets
+are skipped. Invalid rows and stock shortages identify the CSV row and roll
+back the entire import. Consumption is recorded at the sale instant with
+the reference `sale:<ticket>`.
+
+`GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` returns an array ordered
+by `itemId`, with `theoretical`, `actual`, and `difference` (actual minus
+theoretical) in the item's unit. The date range includes both UTC dates.
+Theoretical use comes from sold recipe portions. Actual use includes every
+consume movement in the range. The report includes items with positive use
+in either total.
